1
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:14,980
This card came up very clearly.

2
00:00:16,110 --> 00:00:18,430
It’s about connection,

3
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:20,020
partnership,

4
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:23,100
and two destinies intertwining.

5
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:25,820
Like two timelines crossing?

6
00:00:28,910 --> 00:00:30,430
More like fate crossing.

7
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:36,870
It’s karma from a past life carrying over to the present.

8
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:39,710
I don’t believe in past lives.

9
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:41,850
I live in the present.

10
00:00:51,230 --> 00:00:52,160
Even the present…

11
00:00:53,730 --> 00:00:54,990
isn’t just a coincidence.

12
00:00:56,130 --> 00:00:58,070
When the time comes, you’ll understand.

13
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:01,040
You and he

14
00:01:01,490 --> 00:01:03,910
will shape the past, the present, and the future

15
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:06,060
together.

16
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:29,440
If you don’t confess,

17
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,550
we’ll whip you until you do!

18
00:02:30,550 --> 00:02:33,320
I’m sorry I couldn’t help you.

19
00:02:33,730 --> 00:02:36,860
Just treating my wounds is more than enough.

20
00:02:37,270 --> 00:02:40,290
Why do I keep looking at you

21
00:02:40,650 --> 00:02:43,150
whether you’re asleep or awake?

22
00:02:43,579 --> 00:02:46,960
I hereby appoint you as Phra Sriprach.

23
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:50,370
If I wish to admire the lotus in your hand,

24
00:02:50,370 --> 00:02:52,800
would you allow me?

25
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:31,810
It’s just a market.

26
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:34,079
Why do you look so happy?

27
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:36,870
Of course I am.

28
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:38,940
I don’t get out much.

29
00:03:39,390 --> 00:03:40,730
I’m buried in cases every day.

30
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,490
You know, work and all.

31
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:48,000
I always stay in the same place,

32
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:49,860
and hardly see a place like this.

33
00:03:57,550 --> 00:03:59,150
You seem so easy to please.

34
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:02,500
Just a change of scenery,

35
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:04,770
and you’re already beaming.

36
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:10,550
Maybe I don’t know you well enough.

37
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:15,670
From now on,

38
00:04:16,570 --> 00:04:18,430
I want to get to know you better.

39
00:04:19,649 --> 00:04:20,490
What do you think?

40
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:22,019
Good idea, P'Muen.

41
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:24,460
I want to get to know you too.

42
00:04:26,010 --> 00:04:27,410
Let’s start with something simple.

43
00:04:30,630 --> 00:04:31,470
Food.

44
00:04:32,740 --> 00:04:33,980
What’s your favorite food?

45
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:35,300
Uh…

46
00:04:35,860 --> 00:04:36,960
I love Som Tam.

47
00:04:38,570 --> 00:04:39,540
Som Tam?

48
00:04:40,090 --> 00:04:40,810
What is it?

49
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:44,380
Is it like the Tam Som I know?

50
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:47,860
Then is your Tam Som like the Som Tam I know?

51
00:04:49,570 --> 00:04:51,070
Are you messing with me?

52
00:04:51,730 --> 00:04:52,620
I’m kidding.

53
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:54,380
Som Tam is…

54
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:58,190
shredded green papaya pounded in a mortar,

55
00:04:58,710 --> 00:05:01,380
then add palm sugar, chilies, fish sauce,

56
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:04,160
tomatoes, dried shrimp, and long beans,

57
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,980
and pound everything together.

58
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:08,880
This is making me hungry.

59
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:12,510
You mean Malacca?

60
00:05:13,060 --> 00:05:16,020
Is it the fruit the Dutch brought here?

61
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:18,420
Malacca?

62
00:05:19,130 --> 00:05:20,160
Papaya?

63
00:05:21,010 --> 00:05:21,860
That’s right, P’Muen.

64
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:26,530
So, can your Tam Som beat my Som Tam?

65
00:05:28,490 --> 00:05:31,090
But judging from the name Tam Som,

66
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:34,409
it sounds like a mess, not something tasty.

67
00:05:36,010 --> 00:05:38,810
Tam Som is made with sour fruits,

68
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:44,350
like madan, tamarind, or bilimbi,

69
00:05:45,510 --> 00:05:47,050
and pound them in a mortar.

70
00:05:47,690 --> 00:05:50,380
Then add fish sauce and dried chilies,

71
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:53,050
and keep pounding it all together.

72
00:05:54,159 --> 00:05:56,290
It tastes amazing.

73
00:05:57,300 --> 00:05:58,740
I’m hungry already.

74
00:06:02,350 --> 00:06:03,180
Gaew!

75
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:05,810
Oh, hello, Falcon.

76
00:06:06,470 --> 00:06:08,020
I have something to tell you.

77
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:12,850
Lord Muen.

78
00:06:13,210 --> 00:06:16,070
May I speak with Gaew alone for a moment?

79
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:19,780
Of course. He won’t mind.

80
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:23,300
Go ahead.

81
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:30,030
Maria and I are officially together now.

82
00:06:31,590 --> 00:06:32,590
That's amazing!

83
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:35,750
Congratulations. You finally did it.

84
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:41,970
Keep it a secret for now.

85
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:45,040
Why?

86
00:06:47,190 --> 00:06:49,500
Maria’s father, Fanik,

87
00:06:50,340 --> 00:06:52,900
doesn’t like that I’m from a different faith

88
00:06:53,630 --> 00:06:55,980
and thinks I’m not worthy of his only daughter.

89
00:06:58,150 --> 00:07:00,970
So Maria and I can’t make our relationship public

90
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:03,830
until her father accepts us.

91
00:07:06,390 --> 00:07:07,660
Don’t worry, my lord.

92
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:13,390
You’ll finally be together.

93
00:07:17,550 --> 00:07:18,410
See you around.

94
00:07:26,480 --> 00:07:27,390
Gaew.

95
00:07:27,710 --> 00:07:28,740
What were you talking about?

96
00:07:29,430 --> 00:07:32,540
Why did you have to stand so close and hold hands?

97
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:33,520
Huh?

98
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:36,770
It’s nothing important. Let’s go.

99
00:07:36,940 --> 00:07:37,650
Hey.

100
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:39,290
If it’s not important,

101
00:07:40,210 --> 00:07:41,409
then why did you whisper?

102
00:07:42,470 --> 00:07:45,390
He just doesn't want anyone else to know.

103
00:07:45,650 --> 00:07:46,810
It’s a secret.

104
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:50,530
A secret so big…

105
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:53,180
that you can’t even tell me?

106
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:58,290
Okay, I’ll tell you.

107
00:07:58,860 --> 00:08:00,210
But you can’t tell anyone.

108
00:08:02,570 --> 00:08:06,160
Falcon and Mali are going to be together.

109
00:08:07,470 --> 00:08:09,190
How could they be together?

110
00:08:09,190 --> 00:08:10,060
P’Muen!

111
00:08:10,350 --> 00:08:11,280
It’s a secret.

112
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:12,880
Her father doesn’t approve.

113
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:15,090
How could that happen?

114
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:18,650
They’ll make it work. Trust me.

115
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:22,430
Why are you so sure?

116
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:28,790
You wouldn’t believe me anyway.

117
00:08:29,290 --> 00:08:30,230
I won't say anything.

118
00:08:39,010 --> 00:08:40,240
I’m going to see Mali.

119
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:41,600
P’Yam.

120
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:42,299
Yes, sir.

121
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:53,060
If you use lady finger bananas, it’ll taste sweeter.

122
00:08:53,550 --> 00:08:55,630
Fry them until they’re crispy,

123
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:58,380
then take them out and let the oil drain.

124
00:08:58,990 --> 00:08:59,690
Alright.

125
00:09:03,330 --> 00:09:04,070
Mali.

126
00:09:10,210 --> 00:09:11,700
Falcon just told me.

127
00:09:12,380 --> 00:09:13,350
Congratulations.

128
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:17,410
But…

129
00:09:18,830 --> 00:09:20,180
I know.

130
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:23,700
That’s why I want to cheer you up.

131
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:28,650
Your father may not accept your relationship now,

132
00:09:29,530 --> 00:09:30,670
but one day,

133
00:09:31,310 --> 00:09:35,020
he’ll accept it and let you two get married.

134
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:39,620
I hope you’re right.

135
00:09:43,030 --> 00:09:44,900
Are you in a hurry?

136
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:47,420
No. Why?

137
00:09:49,590 --> 00:09:52,070
I’m teaching her how to make Pisang Goreng.

138
00:09:52,070 --> 00:09:55,070
I wanted you to try some.

139
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:04,800
Pisang goreng?

140
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:08,700
What’s that? I’ve never heard of it.

141
00:10:09,510 --> 00:10:10,830
It’s fried bananas.

142
00:10:11,310 --> 00:10:13,690
I’m teaching her a recipe from the foreigners.

143
00:10:14,010 --> 00:10:17,600
You coat the bananas in batter, then fry them until they’re crispy,

144
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:18,990
and let the oil drain.

145
00:10:21,340 --> 00:10:22,560
Can I try one?

146
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:25,510
I want to see if it tastes like the ones back home.

147
00:10:26,010 --> 00:10:26,770
Of course.

148
00:10:32,430 --> 00:10:33,260
Hm.

149
00:10:34,850 --> 00:10:35,770
So good.

150
00:10:36,910 --> 00:10:38,340
But the name’s a little too hard.

151
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,000
How about this?

152
00:10:40,730 --> 00:10:43,930
Since you got the idea from the foreigners,

153
00:10:44,380 --> 00:10:45,830
why don’t we call it Kluay Khaek?

154
00:10:46,270 --> 00:10:47,900
It’s short and easy to remember.

155
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:49,740
Kluay Khaek?

156
00:10:53,470 --> 00:10:57,820
You know, besides bananas, you can fry other things too.

157
00:10:58,370 --> 00:11:03,050
Like sweet potatoes, taro, pumpkin,

158
00:11:03,820 --> 00:11:04,870
and even pineapple.

159
00:11:05,730 --> 00:11:06,630
Pineapple?

160
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:08,340
Yeah.

161
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:18,210
If you add some coconut and sprinkle a little sesame,

162
00:11:18,550 --> 00:11:19,670
it’ll be really delicious.

163
00:11:26,330 --> 00:11:27,270
Isn’t that strange,

164
00:11:28,450 --> 00:11:29,680
my lord?

165
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:35,740
Lately, Lord Gaew has been interested in cooking,

166
00:11:37,110 --> 00:11:39,450
not sword fighting like before.

167
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:45,110
This Gaew doesn’t seem like the old Gaew.

168
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:03,650
Hey.

169
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:04,910
What is it, P'Muen?

170
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:11,500
Let me see your swordsmanship.

171
00:12:13,330 --> 00:12:14,140
Sure.

172
00:12:19,950 --> 00:12:20,780
Grip.

173
00:12:22,780 --> 00:12:23,620
Lower.

174
00:12:24,900 --> 00:12:28,190
Close, lift, slash, thrust.

175
00:12:29,590 --> 00:12:31,600
Close, lift, dance.

176
00:12:34,030 --> 00:12:36,260
Well, speechless, aren't you?

177
00:12:37,390 --> 00:12:38,980
I just want to spar with you.

178
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:41,100
What kind of stance is that?

179
00:12:41,650 --> 00:12:42,550
So strange.

180
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:46,850
Come on, P’Muen.

181
00:12:47,250 --> 00:12:50,030
This is how I was taught.

182
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:52,320
Stop fooling around.

183
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:54,550
Fight me.

184
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:58,460
Alright.

185
00:13:07,610 --> 00:13:08,540
Get ready!

186
00:13:09,460 --> 00:13:10,180
Come on.

187
00:13:13,710 --> 00:13:14,460
Hey!

188
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:18,880
You’re serious?

189
00:13:19,670 --> 00:13:20,810
That hurts.

190
00:13:21,660 --> 00:13:24,950
You lost because of those weird moves.

191
00:13:26,710 --> 00:13:27,810
In swordsmanship,

192
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:29,980
I am no match for you.

193
00:13:30,620 --> 00:13:31,770
But in horsemanship,

194
00:13:32,590 --> 00:13:34,030
you will surely lose to me.

195
00:13:35,390 --> 00:13:37,100
You can ride a horse?

196
00:13:41,510 --> 00:13:42,450
Want to find out?

197
00:13:43,550 --> 00:13:44,540
Are you challenging me?

198
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:18,910
Are you sure you want to race me?

199
00:14:19,430 --> 00:14:20,480
Absolutely.

200
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:27,520
Is this my horse?

201
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:29,790
Have you lost your mind?

202
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:31,850
That’s P’Sri’s horse.

203
00:14:32,970 --> 00:14:34,260
You’ve never had a horse.

204
00:14:37,490 --> 00:14:38,360
Can you handle it?

205
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:40,510
Just wait and see.

206
00:14:46,070 --> 00:14:46,990
Are you ready?

207
00:14:55,130 --> 00:14:57,250
Hey, that's cheating! Fine, bring it on!

208
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:42,790
What do you think? Am I amazing?

209
00:15:47,390 --> 00:15:48,220
Take the horses back.

210
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:01,580
Gaew.

211
00:16:03,050 --> 00:16:04,250
Who are you?

212
00:16:07,590 --> 00:16:10,100
Did losing make you lose your mind too?

213
00:16:11,810 --> 00:16:13,300
Who are you?

214
00:16:20,340 --> 00:16:22,620
I’m Gaew, your younger brother.

215
00:16:23,630 --> 00:16:24,380
No.

216
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,870
You’re not my younger brother.

217
00:16:36,550 --> 00:16:37,670
I…

218
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:41,910
Dech. Gaew.

219
00:16:43,550 --> 00:16:44,550
Oh, Wad.

220
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:47,510
What brings you here?

221
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:49,510
Nothing.

222
00:16:49,510 --> 00:16:51,420
I just wanted to practice riding too.

223
00:16:51,940 --> 00:16:54,080
How did you know we were here?

224
00:16:54,820 --> 00:16:58,660
The servants told me you were at the stables,

225
00:16:58,940 --> 00:16:59,990
so I followed you.

226
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:02,480
I brought him here to test his riding skills

227
00:17:02,930 --> 00:17:07,829
because he said no one could match him.

228
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:09,329
Yes, sir.

229
00:17:15,410 --> 00:17:16,290
Gaew?

230
00:17:17,339 --> 00:17:18,160
Really?

231
00:17:18,619 --> 00:17:19,339
Yeah.

232
00:17:19,980 --> 00:17:21,150
I even beat P’Muen just now.

233
00:17:22,339 --> 00:17:24,550
Next time, I won’t lose.

234
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:30,290
That sounds like fun.

235
00:17:30,630 --> 00:17:32,450
Mind if I join in?

236
00:17:33,910 --> 00:17:34,790
Sure.

237
00:17:35,940 --> 00:17:37,110
No, I mean…

238
00:17:37,730 --> 00:17:40,890
I want to race against Gaew instead of you.

239
00:17:43,790 --> 00:17:45,200
Is that alright, Gaew?

240
00:17:48,670 --> 00:17:49,650
No problem.

241
00:17:53,170 --> 00:17:54,220
No problem?

242
00:17:55,180 --> 00:17:55,940
What is it?

243
00:17:57,950 --> 00:17:59,710
It means I’m fine with that.

244
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:10,630
Let's let the horses drink some water first.

245
00:18:11,580 --> 00:18:12,480
Sounds good.

246
00:18:19,690 --> 00:18:22,770
Then I'll go water my horse too.

247
00:18:23,790 --> 00:18:24,550
Go ahead.

248
00:19:21,300 --> 00:19:22,770
Are you ready?

249
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:24,380
Gaew.

250
00:19:25,340 --> 00:19:26,210
I've been ready.

251
00:19:32,450 --> 00:19:33,230
Hold on.

252
00:19:34,830 --> 00:19:37,010
Since I'm not racing,

253
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:41,840
can my horse participate in my place?

254
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:42,880
Wait.

255
00:19:43,630 --> 00:19:45,420
Gaew's horse looks much faster.

256
00:19:45,870 --> 00:19:48,800
If he switch horses, he might not be used to it,

257
00:19:49,570 --> 00:19:51,550
and end up losing to me.

258
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:54,060
This isn't my horse.

259
00:19:55,300 --> 00:19:56,200
It belongs to P'Sri.

260
00:19:57,020 --> 00:19:58,030
Besides,

261
00:19:58,640 --> 00:20:01,510
no matter which horse I ride, I'll still win.

262
00:20:04,530 --> 00:20:05,460
Bring it over.

263
00:20:27,580 --> 00:20:28,660
Take good care of Gaew, buddy.

264
00:20:34,230 --> 00:20:34,890
Go!

265
00:21:12,170 --> 00:21:13,020
My lord.

266
00:21:14,180 --> 00:21:15,020
Bring me the horse.

267
00:21:23,630 --> 00:21:24,300
Go!

268
00:21:30,570 --> 00:21:31,380
Ah!

269
00:21:31,380 --> 00:21:32,670
My lord!

270
00:21:35,090 --> 00:21:36,030
My lord!

271
00:21:40,020 --> 00:21:40,750
Stop!

272
00:21:41,580 --> 00:21:42,510
Don't touch him.

273
00:21:54,350 --> 00:21:56,480
P’Pin, bring me two wooden boards.

274
00:21:56,700 --> 00:21:57,980
Let’s take him home.

275
00:21:58,490 --> 00:21:59,220
Yes, sir.

276
00:22:00,750 --> 00:22:01,940
Easy now, P'Muen.

277
00:22:06,330 --> 00:22:09,610
Dech, I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

278
00:22:20,220 --> 00:22:21,110
P'Pin, P'Yam.

279
00:22:21,840 --> 00:22:24,030
Wait outside. I'll take care of him.

280
00:22:24,390 --> 00:22:25,110
Yes, sir.

281
00:22:27,470 --> 00:22:28,190
Go.

282
00:22:29,040 --> 00:22:29,700
Yes, sir.

283
00:22:47,230 --> 00:22:48,660
How are you feeling, P'Muen?

284
00:22:50,530 --> 00:22:51,360
It hurts a lot.

285
00:22:56,770 --> 00:22:58,490
-Easy now.
-What are you doing?

286
00:22:59,850 --> 00:23:00,740
Easy.

287
00:23:01,750 --> 00:23:02,480
Ow!

288
00:23:03,870 --> 00:23:06,430
What are you doing? It hurts!

289
00:23:19,150 --> 00:23:20,090
Ready?

290
00:23:24,570 --> 00:23:26,630
One, two.

291
00:23:33,230 --> 00:23:35,500
Hey, that really hurts.

292
00:23:39,120 --> 00:23:40,190
How does it feel now?

293
00:23:42,900 --> 00:23:43,770
It still hurts.

294
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:48,210
What are you doing?

295
00:23:53,660 --> 00:23:56,310
One, two.

296
00:24:17,810 --> 00:24:18,980
How about now?

297
00:24:20,460 --> 00:24:21,310
Better.

298
00:24:22,670 --> 00:24:23,930
But still hurts.

299
00:24:27,390 --> 00:24:28,540
Easy.

300
00:24:28,540 --> 00:24:29,750
Keep your elbow bent.

301
00:24:31,010 --> 00:24:33,290
Your bone is back in place,

302
00:24:33,290 --> 00:24:36,270
but it still hurts because the muscles are inflamed.

303
00:24:36,980 --> 00:24:38,560
I'll make you a sling,

304
00:24:39,460 --> 00:24:40,860
so your shoulder won’t pop out again.

305
00:25:07,070 --> 00:25:08,590
Keep it like this.

306
00:25:09,270 --> 00:25:10,260
Don't move your arm.

307
00:25:11,050 --> 00:25:12,910
If you don't listen,

308
00:25:13,810 --> 00:25:15,590
and it dislocates again,

309
00:25:15,590 --> 00:25:17,510
I might not be able to fix it.

310
00:25:18,930 --> 00:25:19,950
If you need to bathe,

311
00:25:21,030 --> 00:25:22,080
ask P'Pin to help you.

312
00:25:23,690 --> 00:25:26,150
Or if he can't, I'll do it.

313
00:25:30,630 --> 00:25:31,630
How do you...

314
00:25:33,930 --> 00:25:35,210
know so much about this?

315
00:25:36,550 --> 00:25:39,120
I told you I'm a doctor.

316
00:25:40,990 --> 00:25:41,990
Get some rest.

317
00:25:43,460 --> 00:25:44,220
Gaew.

318
00:25:46,930 --> 00:25:49,870
Thank you for taking good care of me.

319
00:25:50,410 --> 00:25:51,250
You're welcome.

320
00:26:17,980 --> 00:26:19,610
My lord.

321
00:26:20,850 --> 00:26:21,590
What is it?

322
00:26:22,310 --> 00:26:25,810
I have something to tell you about Lord Muen’s accident.

323
00:26:48,320 --> 00:26:49,500
Is something wrong?

324
00:26:51,730 --> 00:26:52,580
Nothing.

325
00:27:00,410 --> 00:27:01,060
Go!

326
00:27:07,350 --> 00:27:08,140
Ah!

327
00:27:08,140 --> 00:27:09,450
My lord!

328
00:27:11,840 --> 00:27:12,740
My lord!

329
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:16,730
Don't touch him.

330
00:27:38,130 --> 00:27:38,900
Wad.

331
00:27:40,270 --> 00:27:41,300
Let’s go to the sword school.

332
00:28:05,660 --> 00:28:06,420
Wad.

333
00:28:07,430 --> 00:28:08,800
I came to return this to you.

334
00:28:16,080 --> 00:28:17,380
It isn’t mine.

335
00:28:18,490 --> 00:28:20,720
Maybe someone dropped it near the stables.

336
00:28:29,900 --> 00:28:31,650
I hadn’t even mentioned the stables.

337
00:28:36,300 --> 00:28:39,740
Was it you who put a nail under my saddle,

338
00:28:40,180 --> 00:28:41,220
and got P’Muen hurt?

339
00:28:44,560 --> 00:28:46,790
Wad would never hurt Dech.

340
00:28:47,750 --> 00:28:49,120
Why would he do that?

341
00:28:50,780 --> 00:28:51,730
Yeah, Wad.

342
00:28:52,550 --> 00:28:53,780
Tell me.

343
00:28:54,670 --> 00:28:57,470
Why did you do it?

344
00:29:00,160 --> 00:29:02,370
How P’Muen would feel if he found out...

345
00:29:02,770 --> 00:29:03,750
his friend did this?

346
00:29:04,540 --> 00:29:06,550
I never meant for Dech to get hurt.

347
00:29:10,670 --> 00:29:13,360
So it’s me you were trying to hurt?

348
00:29:15,600 --> 00:29:16,360
Yes.

349
00:29:17,330 --> 00:29:19,250
I wanted to teach you a lesson.

350
00:29:20,050 --> 00:29:21,020
What lesson?

351
00:29:21,840 --> 00:29:23,200
What’s your problem, Wad?

352
00:29:23,840 --> 00:29:24,980
You’ve gone too far.

353
00:29:25,890 --> 00:29:28,830
What if P’Muen had broken an arm?

354
00:29:30,510 --> 00:29:32,800
I’m sorry Dech got caught in the middle.

355
00:29:33,650 --> 00:29:36,430
I wish it was you instead.

356
00:29:37,030 --> 00:29:37,760
Gaew.

357
00:29:38,630 --> 00:29:40,220
You’re not a real man!

358
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:44,460
Stop it!

359
00:29:44,880 --> 00:29:45,990
That’s enough, Wad. Gaew.

360
00:29:50,320 --> 00:29:51,440
P’Yam, let go.

361
00:30:42,850 --> 00:30:43,610
Wad.

362
00:30:49,420 --> 00:30:50,140
Wait.

363
00:30:50,980 --> 00:30:51,990
Where are you going?

364
00:30:57,390 --> 00:30:58,110
Rueng.

365
00:30:59,050 --> 00:31:02,050
Did you come to gloat over Dech’s accident too?

366
00:31:02,960 --> 00:31:04,230
No.

367
00:31:06,460 --> 00:31:07,120
Wait.

368
00:31:07,840 --> 00:31:08,910
Where are you going?

369
00:31:09,740 --> 00:31:10,580
Home.

370
00:31:11,140 --> 00:31:12,080
I’ll walk you home.

371
00:31:13,130 --> 00:31:15,340
It’s okay, I can get home on my own.

372
00:31:16,150 --> 00:31:17,110
But I want to.

373
00:31:23,890 --> 00:31:25,030
Suit yourself.

374
00:31:37,780 --> 00:31:38,740
Tia.

375
00:31:38,740 --> 00:31:39,710
Yes.

376
00:31:39,710 --> 00:31:40,710
Are you done?

377
00:31:42,500 --> 00:31:43,580
Yes, Your Majesty.

378
00:31:44,190 --> 00:31:46,010
Let Sri read it.

379
00:31:46,250 --> 00:31:47,120
Yes.

380
00:31:55,040 --> 00:31:56,220
Here you go, Sri.

381
00:32:22,650 --> 00:32:24,650
Read this poem.

382
00:32:33,870 --> 00:32:35,100
Go on.

383
00:32:35,770 --> 00:32:36,770
Why are you so quiet?

384
00:32:37,420 --> 00:32:39,050
You wrote this poem, didn’t you?

385
00:32:39,610 --> 00:32:41,980
I could tell at a glance it was yours.

386
00:32:49,770 --> 00:32:51,270
Did you drop it?

387
00:32:56,320 --> 00:32:57,190
Yes.

388
00:33:03,190 --> 00:33:08,800
A graceful beauty, so soft and fair,

389
00:33:11,210 --> 00:33:16,730
So delicate beyond compare.

390
00:33:19,020 --> 00:33:25,750
All who behold you stand in awe,

391
00:33:27,900 --> 00:33:34,670
captivated by your irresistible allure.

392
00:33:38,540 --> 00:33:40,140
This poem is so beautiful.

393
00:33:40,650 --> 00:33:43,610
Don’t you think so, Thao-Srichulaluck?

394
00:33:45,870 --> 00:33:46,580
Yes.

395
00:33:53,900 --> 00:33:55,030
Sriprach.

396
00:34:04,620 --> 00:34:06,740
You are truly a brilliant poet.

397
00:34:10,770 --> 00:34:11,580
See?

398
00:34:12,940 --> 00:34:14,739
Your poetry is dangerously enchanting,

399
00:34:14,739 --> 00:34:16,900
stealing the hearts of countless women.

400
00:34:18,010 --> 00:34:19,120
Even now,

401
00:34:20,389 --> 00:34:22,960
Jam, my consort, is pleased with it.

402
00:34:33,270 --> 00:34:34,030
Sri.

403
00:34:36,020 --> 00:34:36,870
Yes, Your Majesty.

404
00:34:38,389 --> 00:34:40,719
Your poem is exquisite, Sri.

405
00:34:45,770 --> 00:34:48,199
Thank you, Your Majesty. It is my greatest honor.

406
00:36:37,390 --> 00:36:41,940
My thoughts are bound to your noble grace.

407
00:36:44,010 --> 00:36:48,160
While I grieve in my lowly place.

408
00:36:50,310 --> 00:36:52,140
Of all the souls to love,

409
00:36:54,180 --> 00:36:55,730
I fall for one forbidden.

410
00:37:02,140 --> 00:37:04,100
I am but dust beneath your feet,

411
00:37:05,670 --> 00:37:06,630
unworthy of

412
00:37:08,570 --> 00:37:09,490
heaven above.

413
00:37:11,110 --> 00:37:12,240
Sri, you fool.

414
00:37:14,270 --> 00:37:16,940
His Majesty has only shown you love and kindness.

415
00:37:21,490 --> 00:37:24,460
How could you even think of betraying him?

416
00:37:31,450 --> 00:37:32,290
P’Sri.

417
00:37:43,080 --> 00:37:43,950
P’Sri.

418
00:37:45,830 --> 00:37:47,370
I heard that

419
00:37:48,450 --> 00:37:50,710
you’re about to be promoted to Lord Phra Sriprach.

420
00:37:58,510 --> 00:37:59,390
So…

421
00:38:00,830 --> 00:38:02,120
Congratulations.

422
00:38:04,530 --> 00:38:06,350
But do you mind if I say something?

423
00:38:10,050 --> 00:38:11,940
When you become Sriprach,

424
00:38:13,070 --> 00:38:15,620
I hope you’ll think carefully

425
00:38:16,580 --> 00:38:18,430
about who you choose to love.

426
00:38:20,370 --> 00:38:21,820
Don’t fall for someone

427
00:38:22,860 --> 00:38:24,380
who already belongs to another

428
00:38:25,870 --> 00:38:27,380
or is already married.

429
00:38:32,050 --> 00:38:33,250
I just want to warn you.

430
00:38:56,010 --> 00:38:57,660
Lord Phra Sriprach has arrived.

431
00:39:07,460 --> 00:39:09,410
I must have been blind.

432
00:39:12,910 --> 00:39:14,310
Otherwise, I would’ve known that

433
00:39:14,960 --> 00:39:16,880
the man standing before me

434
00:39:17,890 --> 00:39:19,750
is the kingdom’s greatest poet

435
00:39:21,820 --> 00:39:23,900
and His Majesty’s favorite.

436
00:39:25,500 --> 00:39:27,190
Please forgive me.

437
00:39:28,740 --> 00:39:30,540
Last time, I didn’t know my place

438
00:39:31,210 --> 00:39:33,450
and dared to speak with Thao-Srichulaluck,

439
00:39:34,540 --> 00:39:36,370
His Majesty’s royal consort.

440
00:39:38,030 --> 00:39:39,830
We didn’t know each other.

441
00:39:41,150 --> 00:39:42,540
What happened back then

442
00:39:43,230 --> 00:39:44,940
wasn’t anyone’s fault.

443
00:39:48,550 --> 00:39:49,850
But this time,

444
00:39:51,610 --> 00:39:53,750
we both know

445
00:39:54,940 --> 00:39:57,610
that our duty is to remain loyal

446
00:39:58,950 --> 00:40:00,940
and faithful to the king.

447
00:40:02,330 --> 00:40:03,200
Isn’t that right?

448
00:40:06,780 --> 00:40:07,580
Yes.

449
00:40:13,520 --> 00:40:15,190
Hurry back to serve His Majesty.

450
00:40:18,750 --> 00:40:20,120
Please allow me to take my leave.

451
00:40:49,090 --> 00:40:50,460
This is for you.

452
00:40:51,310 --> 00:40:53,620
Go back and take care of your mother’s funeral, P’Yam.

453
00:40:56,850 --> 00:40:57,750
Take it.

454
00:41:01,670 --> 00:41:03,910
And don’t worry about me.

455
00:41:04,420 --> 00:41:05,580
I can take care of myself.

456
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:06,700
Yes, sir.

457
00:41:08,220 --> 00:41:09,300
Are you going alone?

458
00:41:10,560 --> 00:41:11,840
Why don’t you take P’Pin with you?

459
00:41:12,550 --> 00:41:14,010
I did,

460
00:41:14,010 --> 00:41:16,070
but I don’t know if Lord Muen will allow it.

461
00:41:17,190 --> 00:41:17,850
No.

462
00:41:20,740 --> 00:41:21,820
Pin.

463
00:41:22,250 --> 00:41:23,210
If you’re not here,

464
00:41:24,050 --> 00:41:25,220
who’s going to grind my ink

465
00:41:25,760 --> 00:41:26,940
and help me bathe?

466
00:41:27,930 --> 00:41:28,820
Pee and poop too.

467
00:41:29,580 --> 00:41:30,820
How am I supposed to do that?

468
00:41:31,620 --> 00:41:32,540
But I…

469
00:41:32,540 --> 00:41:33,820
Am I not making myself clear?

470
00:41:34,480 --> 00:41:35,350
Loud and clear, sir.

471
00:41:36,080 --> 00:41:38,310
You’re so mean.

472
00:41:40,780 --> 00:41:41,840
Is that all?

473
00:41:42,690 --> 00:41:43,920
I’ll help you myself.

474
00:41:50,670 --> 00:41:51,440
Okay.

475
00:41:53,540 --> 00:41:54,740
What does “okay” mean?

476
00:41:56,050 --> 00:41:57,200
It means “agreed.”

477
00:41:58,450 --> 00:41:59,570
Thank you, my lord.

478
00:42:00,570 --> 00:42:02,470
Hurry up. Yam must be waiting for you.

479
00:42:02,970 --> 00:42:03,770
-Yes, sir.
-Go.

480
00:42:15,540 --> 00:42:16,750
You’re acting all cool.

481
00:42:22,460 --> 00:42:23,280
Ow.

482
00:42:28,170 --> 00:42:29,470
Ow, Pin!

483
00:42:30,210 --> 00:42:30,980
Pin!

484
00:42:36,590 --> 00:42:37,460
What do you want?

485
00:42:38,810 --> 00:42:40,000
I want to grind the ink.

486
00:42:52,250 --> 00:42:53,230
Can you help me?

487
00:43:05,570 --> 00:43:06,470
What are you looking at?

488
00:43:08,270 --> 00:43:09,300
Do I have ink on my face?

489
00:43:12,330 --> 00:43:13,060
No.

490
00:43:14,400 --> 00:43:15,570
I wasn’t looking.

491
00:43:30,410 --> 00:43:31,250
It’s done.

492
00:43:40,180 --> 00:43:41,620
Can you hand me the quill?

493
00:43:43,250 --> 00:43:44,100
The quill?

494
00:43:44,550 --> 00:43:45,140
There.

495
00:43:46,450 --> 00:43:47,050
Please.

496
00:43:53,280 --> 00:43:54,170
Quill?

497
00:44:16,210 --> 00:44:16,820
Come on.

498
00:44:17,900 --> 00:44:18,940
I’ll help you.

499
00:44:27,130 --> 00:44:28,060
Where do I write?

500
00:44:29,530 --> 00:44:31,340
The second line.

501
00:44:32,000 --> 00:44:33,040
You can use that hand?

502
00:44:33,900 --> 00:44:34,660
Ow!

503
00:44:35,530 --> 00:44:37,030
This side hurts too.

504
00:44:41,190 --> 00:44:41,820
Come here.

505
00:45:19,530 --> 00:45:20,620
Are you coming with me?

506
00:45:21,090 --> 00:45:21,740
Yeah.

507
00:45:22,100 --> 00:45:23,250
I don’t want you to be alone.

508
00:45:29,900 --> 00:45:32,910
Thanks for coming with me.

509
00:45:36,390 --> 00:45:38,670
I’ve packed some cooked rice and dried fish.

510
00:45:39,660 --> 00:45:40,670
We can eat on the way.

511
00:45:49,420 --> 00:45:50,260
Let’s go.

512
00:45:50,590 --> 00:45:51,230
Come on.

513
00:46:04,460 --> 00:46:05,230
Gaew.

514
00:46:05,710 --> 00:46:06,330
Yes?

515
00:46:08,940 --> 00:46:10,060
Help me take off my shirt.

516
00:46:10,990 --> 00:46:11,910
I want to take a bath.

517
00:47:00,820 --> 00:47:02,410
How’s your arm?

518
00:47:03,210 --> 00:47:04,260
Much better.

519
00:47:18,260 --> 00:47:19,020
Gaew.

520
00:47:19,580 --> 00:47:20,450
Go take a bath.

521
00:48:59,830 --> 00:49:02,060
I wish I could bathe with you like this

522
00:49:02,860 --> 00:49:03,940
every day.

523
00:49:06,370 --> 00:49:07,260
You can.

524
00:50:03,930 --> 00:50:05,430
Overall, his condition is stable.

525
00:50:05,830 --> 00:50:07,470
His blood pressure and pulse are normal.

526
00:50:07,990 --> 00:50:09,840
But we still can’t determine

527
00:50:09,840 --> 00:50:11,420
why he hasn’t regained consciousness.

528
00:50:14,190 --> 00:50:15,140
It may be

529
00:50:16,000 --> 00:50:17,190
acute shock.

530
00:50:25,590 --> 00:50:26,500
Thank you very much.

531
00:50:28,790 --> 00:50:29,980
Thank you, doctor.

532
00:50:41,520 --> 00:50:43,620
Rich, you have to help him.

533
00:50:49,380 --> 00:50:50,950
No matter what’s wrong with Great,

534
00:50:50,950 --> 00:50:52,300
or how hard it is.

535
00:50:52,950 --> 00:50:54,810
Please do your best to help him.

536
00:50:57,100 --> 00:50:58,780
Even if I have to sell my resort,

537
00:50:59,580 --> 00:51:00,560
I’ll do it.

538
00:51:03,100 --> 00:51:04,000
Yes, Grandma.

539
00:51:20,010 --> 00:51:21,330
What’s gotten into you two?

540
00:51:21,330 --> 00:51:22,850
One’s heart is burning with love,

541
00:51:22,850 --> 00:51:24,340
while the other’s hiding it deeply.

542
00:51:24,530 --> 00:51:26,060
Maybe Lord Sriprach

543
00:51:26,060 --> 00:51:29,780
has fallen for someone who’s already taken.

544
00:51:30,070 --> 00:51:33,140
Politics won’t be your downfall,

545
00:51:33,140 --> 00:51:34,420
but love will.

546
00:51:35,260 --> 00:51:37,060
You’ve fallen for someone, haven’t you?

547
00:51:37,450 --> 00:51:38,650
Do you really want to know?

548
00:51:39,110 --> 00:51:42,450
Then, go look into a looking glass,

549
00:51:42,450 --> 00:51:43,780
and you shall find the answer.
